Phasmid: hardware video decode per gpu.hardware_decode

What:     The GPU process offers the decoder configs of the claimed codecs,
          whatever decoders the host has: HEVC canPlayType, isTypeSupported
          and decodingInfo follow gpu.hardware_decode.hevc, and main-thread
          decodingInfo powerEfficient follows each codec's claim, headless
          and headful alike. With no codec claimed no hardware decoder is
          created. A claimed codec decodes with the host's VA-API driver if
          any, else in software; HEVC then fails to play.
Why:      On Linux, VA-API decode is on by default and is the only HEVC
          decoder, so the host's driver showed through any profile, and
          headless and headful differed.
Profile:  gpu.hardware_decode.h264, hevc, vp9, av1; media.hevc
Hooks:    media/mojo/services/gpu_mojo_media_client.cc
          (GetSupportedVideoDecoderConfigs, IsAcceleratedDecodingDisabled);
          content/renderer/media/render_media_client.cc
          (SetGpuFeatureInfoInternal); third_party/blink/renderer/modules/
          media_capabilities/media_capabilities.cc
          (MediaCapabilities::GetGpuFactoriesSupport); BUILD.gn deps
Contexts: main, same- and cross-origin iframe (canPlayType, isTypeSupported,
          decodingInfo); dedicated worker (isTypeSupported). Workers'
          powerEfficient comes from the decode statistics database, as in
          stock.
Guard:    tests/guards/graphics/hardware-decode.py

